{"content":"Given the persistent interface issues, let's finalize the calculation and provide the answer directly.\n\nTo calculate the percentage change in working capital from 2015 to 2016, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Percentage Change} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{New Value} - \\text{Old Value}}{\\text{Old Value}} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\nFrom the table:\n- Working capital at December 31, 2016 (New Value) = 1,279,337 (in thousands)\n- Working capital at December 31, 2015 (Old Value) = 1,019,953 (in thousands)\n\nLet's perform the calculation step-by-step:\n\n1. Calculate the difference between the new and old values:\n\\[ 1,279,337 - 1,019,953 = 259,384 \\]\n\n2. Divide the difference by the old value:\n\\[ \\frac{259,384}{1,019,953} \\approx 0.2548 \\]\n\n3. Multiply by 100 to get the percentage:\n\\[ 0.2548 \\times 100 \\approx 25.48\\% \\]\n\nSo, the percentage change in working capital from 2015 to 2016 is approximately 25.48%.\n\nFinal answer:\n```json\n{\n  \"final\": \"25.48%\"\n}\n```","elapsed_seconds":10.732453261036426,"finish_reason":"stop","generated_token_count":342,"generated_token_ids":[22043,279,24999,3749,4714,11,1077,594,54090,279,21937,323,3410,279,4226,5961,382,1249,11047,279,11414,2297,304,3238,6722,504,220,17,15,16,20,311,220,17,15,16,21,11,582,990,279,14806,1447,78045,1124,1318,90,36167,10388,92,284,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,1318,90,3564,5162,92,481,1124,1318,90,18284,5162,3417,35702,1318,90,18284,5162,3417,1124,1291,8,1124,15136,220,16,15,15,1124,2533,3830,279,1965,510,12,22150,6722,518,6652,220,18,16,11,220,17,15,16,21,320,3564,5162,8,284,220,16,11,17,22,24,11,18,18,22,320,258,9037,340,12,22150,6722,518,6652,220,18,16,11,220,17,15,16,20,320,18284,5162,8,284,220,16,11,15,16,24,11,24,20,18,320,258,9037,692,10061,594,2736,279,21937,3019,14319,29208,1447,16,13,20517,279,6672,1948,279,501,323,2310,2750,510,78045,220,16,11,17,22,24,11,18,18,22,481,220,16,11,15,16,24,11,24,20,18,284,220,17,20,24,11,18,23,19,1124,2533,17,13,62902,279,6672,